From d1fc13f96f5b2613d4b639e9ebf9b6b9c2099ee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:26:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 44/60] Muse Spark: the DFlash2 drafter (RadixArk
 Muse-Spark-Open-DFlash2), EXL3 pack, split under TP=2

dflash2_config.zig: the drafter's config (5 sliding-window GQA layers, block 8, taps after target layers
1/16/30/44/59, selector rank 256 / top 16, grouped dynamic causal convolutions) and its per-rank cuts (q/o by
heads, k/v by KV heads, MLP by width, fc by outputs). dflash2.zig: the drafter fed from inside the target's run
(residual taps, then the context K/V update after the last layer), a draft pass per stream count that captures as a
CUDA graph (up to 16 streams x 8 rows). The MiMo-V2 DFlash kernels are reused for embedding, taps, per-head norm
and RoPE, cache stores, block attention and row takes; muse_spark/dflash2.cu adds the selector's dense projection,
the conv prepare/finish, SiLU-mul, the per-rank top 16 of the scaled, softcapped head and the candidate walk.
